      "source": "https://www.avocaarkansas.gov/about/about.aspx"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Avoca means 'the gathering place' in Native American tradition and was named after the Irish town of Avoca.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.avocaarkansas.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1920 Avoca had become a booming town serving the area as a freight and passenger train stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.avocaarkansas.gov/about/about.aspx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office called Avoca has been in operation in the town since 1872.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
